{"name":"Light Cuddle","hex":"#cbd7ed","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"cuddle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An intimate physical embrace, typically while lying (or sitting): a snuggle, an instance of lying together snugly, as one might with a partner (more intimate than a hug, and typically of longer duration).","An affectionate embrace, a hug, such as is given to family members and close friends (less intimate than a snuggle, and typically of shorter duration)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lie together snugly (with someone), in an intimate physical embrace; to snuggle.","To embrace (someone) affectionately; to hug (someone) closely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cuddle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hug","blocks":[{"text":"A hug is a form of endearment, found in virtually all human communities, in which two or more people put their arms around the neck, back, under the armpits or waists of one another and hold each other closely. If more than two people are involved, it may be referred to as a group hug."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Wedding_hugs.jpg/330px-Wedding_hugs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hug","wikidata":"Q328703"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG/500px-A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG/1280px-A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG/500px-A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Yoruba bride and mother","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg/500px-2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg/1280px-2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg/500px-2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-0